1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Predecessor:'''[]<br/>
2 CONT '''Successor:'''[]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Tewodros II (ቴዎድሮስ)''', baptized as '''Sahle Dingil'''; c. 1818 – April 13, 1868 was Emperor of Ethiopia from 1855 until his death. He was born '''Kassa Hailegiorgis ( ካሳ ኃይሉ)'''. His rule is often placed as the beginning of mo
2 CONC dern Ethiopia, ending the decentralized Zemene Mesafint (Era of the Princes).
2 CONT
2 CONT Tewodros II's origins were in the Era of the Princes, but his ambitions were not those of the regional nobility. He sought to reestablish a cohesive Ethiopian state and to reform its administration and church. He sought to restore
2 CONC  Solomonic hegemony, and he considered himself the Elect of God.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tewodros II's first task was to bring Shewa under his control. During the Era of the Princes, Shewa was, even more than most provinces, an independent entity, its ruler even styling himself Negus, a royal title denoting monarchy. 
2 CONC In the course of subduing the Shewans, Tewodros imprisoned a Shewan prince, [https://www.geni.com/people/Emperor-Menelik-II/6000000009686681685 Menelik II], who would later become emperor himself. Despite his success against Shewa
2 CONC , Tewodros faced constant rebellions in other provinces.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.britannica.com/biography/Tewodros-II Brittanica:Tewdoros II]<br/>
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tewodros_II Wikipedia:Tewdoros II]
