1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Shumye Guangul left Woldia when he was young and moved to Addis to be with his distant relative Gugsa Wole (with whom he grew up). The latter was the son of Welle Betul who was the ruler of Yejju and Simien, and br
2 CONC other of Empress Tayitu. Gugsa Wole married Empress Zewditu before she was crowned, in a marriage that was arranged by Empress Tayitu to extend her influence through her nephew. When he married, Gugsa Wole was promoted to the Ras 
2 CONC over Begemder Province. They were happily married until Zewditu's coronation which was arranged by Ras Teferi, who became the Crown Prince and later became Emperor Haile Selassie. He forced Ras Gugsa to leave Addis to govern Begem
2 CONC der and live in Dere Tabor (the capital of the province). Shumye who was the assistant of the Ras at he time went with him. They governed Begemder for many years until the Ras declared war against the Shewan oligarchy because he s
2 CONC aw himself as the future emperor instead of Haile Selassie and also because he became tired of living separated from his wife Empress Zewditu. Shumye Guangul was appointed as the army leader. They fought with great bravery and det
2 CONC ermination to win until the Shewan oligarchy used a military plane to  drop bombs from the sky, which was never seen before in the country. This was indeed the first time a military plane was used in Ethiopia.
2 CONT The Ras was killed in the war and Shumye Guangul was captured and imprisoned for over 8 years until the Italians invaded Ethiopia. Empress Zewditu died of heartbreak 3 days after hearing the news of her husband's death.
