1 NOTE Farmed 500 acres. Was an owner of the Hampton Cheese Factory. WasSupervisor of Hampton 1871, 1874, and 1875. Was Property Assessor1876. Squire's farm is in the possession of Richard Miley, Squire'sgreat grandson (1964).
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 census shows Squire and Mary living in Kingsbury, NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Have seen this name written as "Esquire Able".
2 CONT
2 CONT 1864. Squire was appointed on a committee to fill the quota ofrecruits for the Cival War.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Race family recordes Squire was married twice, but the2nd wife's name is not given. There is a record in the Hampton clerk'sregister of the death of Cordelia Warren, daughter of Roswell Place.This is possilby Squire's
2 CONC  2nd wife. One member of the family statedthat Squire's 2nd wife was a "witch and possibly deranged". This mayexplain why so little information is given in the Race book.
2 CONT
