2 CONC on the Missouri River, Knife Riverregion. James bought a large amount of land and operated a horse andcattle ranch on an extensive scale until 1906, when he retired fromactive business and spent his later life in Stanley. His wife
2 CONC  died onthe ranch in 1904. They had 12 children, 7 daughters, 5 sons. Historyof ND, 1931 by Lewis Crawford, library no. 978.4 / C957 / V3.
2 CONT
2 CONT James was known as J.W. Warren.
2 CONT
