1 FAMS @F6000000001510678667@
1 RFN geni:6000000007453845501
1 SUBM @S6000000001510419741@
1 NOTE Possibly "Squire Arthur" & was written down wrong [?].
2 CONT
2 CONT Kept wild animals. A monkey, wolf, cougar cubs.
2 CONT
2 CONT           INFORMATION FROM 1920 SOUNDEX [W650]
2 CONT Found "Squire" A. Warren on 1920 Soundex. Ordered 1920 Census#1821337.
2 CONT [Vol. 16; E.D. 163; sheet 10; line 87.
2 CONT On the 1920 Soundex, the daughters ages given are wrong.
2 CONT Birth certificates verify the ages on this program as correct.
2 CONT Family lived on Moran Street, & had 1 lodger.
2 CONT
2 CONT            INFORMATION FROM 1920 CENSUS
2 CONT Listed all of living family. Square Arthur's occupation in 1920 was amail carrier.
2 CONT
2 CONT SA Warren attended common schools and finished his education in theMayville Normal school. He assisted his father on the ranch until themove to Stanley, where for 22 years he conducted a transfer and housemoving business.  SA Warr
2 CONC en was a member of the Stanley CommercialClub.  He was affiliated with the Masonic Fraternity and Eastern Star,the Independent Order of Odd Fellows, the Woodmen of the World and wasa member of the Presbyterian Church. He was first
2 CONC  elected sheriff ofMountrail county in 1926 and then re-elected in 1928. [from Crawford'sHistory of ND., v 3, pg 582.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1885 - Moved to Dakota Territory.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dec. 1904  - S. A. Warrens's house, that had been used as a schoolburned to the ground.
2 CONT 1907 -  He was working as an excavator.
2 CONT April, 1908 - S.A. purchased the "fine large dwelling house of O.P.Olson, located on 2nd street in the east part of town." (Stanley Sun,April 3, 1908)
2 CONT May 22, 1908 - SA elected as Trustee, 2nd Ward, with 62 votes. Papersaid that "S. Warren ia all right!  He is a trustworthy young man."
2 CONT
