1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ancestor #: A121492
2 CONT
2 CONT Service Source:  GOODRICH, ROLLS OF THE SOLS IN THE REV WAR 1775-1783, PP 182, 587, 682, 787, 795, 814-815
2 CONT Service Description:  1) ALSO LT; LCOL SETH WARNER, COL ETHAN ALLEN, GREEN MOUNTAIN BOYS,
2 CONT 2) COL, 3RD & 15TH VT REGTS\\
2 CONT Commnts on file: CALEB D, ASA & SARA WERE CHILDREN OF ANNA BISHOP
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Col Gideon Warren
2 CONT BIRTH	12 Dec 1730, Brimfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT DEATH	4 Apr 1803 (aged 72), Hampton, Washington County, New York, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	Hampton Hill Cemetery, Hampton, Washington County, New York, USA, MEMORIAL ID 20475962 , Photos by Janet Muff¡
2 CONT
2 CONT He served in the Revolutionary War as a Colonel with the Green Mountain Boys, and was injured at Fort Ticonderoga. His military and political activities are well documented in the published literature, both historical and genealog
2 CONC ical. Here is an excerpt from a contributor concerning his military activities:
2 CONT
2 CONT His record shows that he fought in the French and Indian War because it contains an application for a bounty for an Indian scalp, a customary procedure for proving involvement in the French and Indian War. He continued his service
2 CONC  in the militia and was later elected a Lieutenant in Ethan Allen’s Green Mountain Boys. His records also show that he was present at the taking of Fort Ticonderoga, New York on May 10, 1775; he remained at Fort Ticonderoga as par
2 CONC t of the garrison.
2 CONT
2 CONT At some later date he was seriously injured by the stoke of a machete type cutlass to the wrist. The injury was so bad that it almost cut his hand off entirely. This all occurred when he and others tried to disarm a soldier who wa
2 CONC s either a madman or a Tory. The soldier had gathered a selection of weapons and Warren and others were attempting to disarm him when the injury took place. The wound was serious enough to disqualify him from any more active duty 
2 CONC and he was no longer capable of obtaining his livelihood by labor and became a Colonel in the Vermont Militia. (Courtesy of Post44 Bantam (50707891)¡
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT In 
2 CONT Memory of 
2 CONT Col. 
2 CONT GIDEON WARREN
2 CONT who died April 4th 
2 CONT 1803
2 CONT in the 73d year of 
2 CONT his age.
2 CONT
2 CONT An angels arm can't snatch 
2 CONT me from the grave. 
2 CONT Legions of angels can't confine
2 CONT me there.
2 CONT
