1 NOTE 1st wife Ann Bishop.  2nd wife Eunice Chipman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. Gideon was charged with the task of confiscating Loyalistproperty for the support of the wartime militia, but had sympathy forthose Loyalists with families who remained on their property while thehead of the household was  aw
2 CONC ay. [See letter from David Goff, under`Warrens I'].
2 CONT
2 CONT Helped build Fort Warren. Had a hand in laying the foundation ofWilliamstown. Gideon Warren was a Capt. when he helped with thevictory at Fort Ticonderoga, and was a member of Ethan Allen's GreenMountain Boys.
2 CONT
2 CONT On may 28, 1778, the 5th Regiment of 16 Companies was organized andGideon was commissioned Colonel in Command.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was in June 1778 that Gideon was chosen for Justice of the Peacefor Tinmouth.
2 CONT
2 CONT A history of Hampton, NY states that Col. Gideon Warren gave land forthe first church, first school, and the first cemetary next to thechurch. Gideon's gravestone inscription reads: "In memory of Col.Gideon Warren who died in Apri
2 CONC l 4, 1803 in the 73rd year of his age."On the lower part of the stone the following appears: "An angel's armscan't snatch me from the grave - Legions of angels can't confine methere." At the foot of the grave is a small stone mark
2 CONC ed simply:"C.W."
2 CONT
2 CONT LDS ORDINANCES: Gideon work was also done at the Ogden Temple beforewe found out that the work was previously done. We did it on June 5,1993 at Ogden.
2 CONT
2 CONT An extract of Gideon Warren's Last Will and Testament is located atthe:
2 CONT Surrogates Office, Court House, Salem, New York.
2 CONT Wills: Book II, Page 25.  Recorded 25 July, 1803.
2 CONT
