1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ancestor #: A204179
2 CONT Service:  VERMONT    Rank(s): NON-COMMISSIONED OFFICER
2 CONT
2 CONT David Bishop Warren
2 CONT BIRTH	1764, Vermont, USA
2 CONT DEATH	22 Mar 1829 (aged 64–65), Hampton, Washington County, New York, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	Hampton Hill Cemetery, Hampton, Washington County, New York, USA
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID 40551796, Photos by Jill_R
2 CONT
2 CONT David Bishop Warren, Sr., was born abt 1764, probably in Sunderland in the Hampshire Grants (now VT). 
2 CONT
2 CONT His father, Gideon Warren, was Capt. in the Green Mountain Boys, and Colonel of the 15th VT Militia during the Revolutionary War. Col. Warren superintended the building of Ft. Warren in Castleton, VT, and was wounded in the elbow 
2 CONC at the taking of Ft. Ticonderoga on 10 May 1775. His mother was likely Anna Bishop, daughter of David Bishop of Sturbridge MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT David Bishop Warren was a fifer and later, a non commissioned officer,  in Ebenezer Allen's Regt. during the War. He married Grace Fletcher of Poultney VT in the Spring of 1784. They resided in Poultney until abt. 1788, when he to
2 CONC ok the Freeman's Oath in South Hero, VT. By Spring 1793, he began selling his land in South Hero, and he and his family of 8 children, went by boat up Lake Champlain into Canada. We first find him owning land in Buckingham Twp, Qu
2 CONC ebec, on the Grand (now Ottawa) River north and slightly east of Ottawa. Next we find him in Hawkesbury, Prescott Co. Ontario. By 1810 he had purchased land in South Crosby, Leeds Co. Ontario, where he farmed until Oct. 1828, when
2 CONC  he deeded his farm to son, Artemas Warren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT David Bishop Warren returned to the home of family in Hampton, NY, after that date. A funeral service for him was conducted at the Christ Church in Hampton on 22 Mar 1829. He is buried near the grave of his father, Gideon, and his
2 CONC  brother Caleb Warren. His wife, Grace Fletcher Warren, predeceased him, most likely in South Crosby, Ontario, but no grave for her has been found.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT Gideon Warren
2 CONT 1730–1803
2 CONT Ann Warren
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings
2 CONT Caleb Warren
2 CONT 1763–1846
2 CONT Asa Warren
2 CONT 1766–1807
2 CONT Ebenezer Warren
2 CONT 1767–1840
2 CONT Half Siblings
2 CONT Sarah Warren Webster
2 CONT 1769–1813
2 CONT Elizabeth Warren Webster
2 CONT 1771–1848
2 CONT Clorinda Warren Knapp
2 CONT 1784–1853
2 CONT Ammi Warren
2 CONT 1790–1859
2 CONT Gideon Chipman Warren
2 CONT 1792–1875
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT David Bishop Warren
2 CONT 1797–1855
2 CONT
