1 TITL Pvt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of Pliney Price & Betsy Eliza (Willis) Warren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Enlisted as a Private on August 9, 1862 at the age of 28. Joined Co. H, 38th Iowa Infantry Regiment on November 4, 1862.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died of disease on November 27, 1863 at Brownsville, TX. Originally buried at Brownsville National Cemetery in Brownsville, TX. In 1911, the cemetery was closed and over 1,500 Union soldier remains were removed and re-interred in 
2 CONC a single grave at Alexandria National Cemetery in Pineville, LA. Pvt. Abel Warren is believed to be among them. Note: There is no individual marker for his grave. He is believed to be buried among the unknowns.
