1 NOTE Stephen Payne
2 CONT Stephen Payne was born in Grand Isle Co., VT. on 28 Oct 1799 to
2 CONT Daniel Payne and an as yet unknown mother. At a very young age he
2 CONT served as a fifer in the War of 1812.
2 CONT In 1827 he married Rhoda Place . They had four children: Edwin
2 CONT (1829, NY) Edgar (c1830, CN), Charity (c1832, NY), and Lucinda (c1834,
2 CONT NY).
2 CONT Shortly after Lucinda was born, Stephen and family moved to Canada
2 CONT and lived there until 1839 when they moved to Huron County, Ohio. The
2 CONT family lived in Huron Co. for about five years. Rhoda Payne died on 15
2 CONT Mar 1842. (The 1840 census shows Stephen Payne with a household
2 CONT consisting of 2 males ages 10-15, one male age 30-40, 2 females age
2 CONT 5-10 and one female age 30-40.)
2 CONT In 1842, Stephen Payne re-married, this time to a Mrs. Adelia
2 CONT Gaylord, and, in 1844 they moved to Bloominggrove Twp, Richland County
2 CONT and settled in the village of Ganges. Adelia Payne died in 1869 and at
2 CONT that time Stephen moved to Shiloh to live with his son Edgar, who was
2 CONT a blacksmith there. In July of 1876 Stephen travelled to Galion, Ohio
2 CONT in Crawford County to visit his daughter Charity and her husband
2 CONT Joseph Funk. While there his health failed him and he died on 20 Aug
2 CONT 1876.
2 CONT From the records of the Crawford County, Ohio Probate Court:
2 CONT Full Name: Payne Steven; Date of Death: August 20 1876; Place of
2 CONT Death: Galion, Ohio; Condition: Wid'd; Age: 77; Place of Birth:
2 CONT Vermont; Occupation: Blacksmith; Name of Parents: Daniel Payne/Unk;
2 CONT Disease: Inf of Bowels; Color: White;   Last Residence: Galion, Ohio
