1 NOTE Edwin R. Payne (1829-1892)
2 CONT In the summer of 1862, Edwin Payne of Richland County, Ohio,
2 CONT enlisted in the Union army. He served in the 82nd regiment, Company F,
2 CONT of the Ohio Volunteer Infantry. According to the Civil War Roster,
2 CONT found in the Western Reserve Historical Society library, vol. 6 p538,
2 CONT he entered service on 28 Aug. 1862 and served for three years. He was
2 CONT appointed corporal (date unkn) and was mustered out on 10 June 1865
2 CONT "near Washington, D.C., by order of the War Dept."
2 CONT The Civil War Roster gives a list of the battles fought by the 82nd
2 CONT Ohio Regiment. These include: 2nd Bull Run (8/28-8/30/1862);
2 CONT Chancellorsville, VA (5/1-5/6/1863) [as part of the "infamous"
2 CONT Eleventh Army Corps]; Gettysburg, PA (7/1-7/3 1863) [Cemetary Hill];
2 CONT Wauhatchie, TN (10/27-10/28 1863); Missionary Ridge, TN (11/22-11/26
2 CONT 1863); Knoxville, TN; Resaca, GA; New Hope Church, GA; Culp's Farm,
2 CONT GA; Peach Tree Creek, GA; Atlanta GA (7/23-10/2 1864); March To The
2 CONT Sea; Sandersville, GA; Averysboro, NC; Bentonville, NC
2 CONT (3/19-3/21/1865)
2 CONT The following is a verbatim transcript of the obituary for Edwin Payne
2 CONT which appeared in the Mansfield "Richland Shield and Banner" on
2 CONT Saturday 23 Jan 1892.
2 CONT "Edwin Payne Dead"
2 CONT The Ex-Infirmary Director Dies Last Night"
2 CONT "It is with much regret that the SHIELD chronicles the death of
2 CONT Edwin Payne, that sterling Democrat and ex-Infirmary Director. Mr.
2 CONT Payne died at his residence in Shelby at 4 o'clock last evening of
2 CONT paralysis, having sustained five strokes of the affliction within the
2 CONT past five months, the last one being about ten days ago. Since
2 CONT Saturday, January 9th, until the time of his death, Mr. Payne had not
2 CONT eaten a mouthful of solid food. The trouble had also affected him to
2 CONT such an extent that he was unable to see or talk. The muscles of the
2 CONT entire body seemed to paralyzed (sic) in the last attack and his
2 CONT internal organs refused to perform their respective duties. Hence, his
2 CONT death yesterday was a relief to the sufferer, although an additional
2 CONT affliction to his friends and relatives."
2 CONT "The deceased was born in Pennsylvania sixty-three years ago. While
2 CONT still a small boy his parents removed to the northern part of this
2 CONT county, where Mr. Payne has since lived. In 1887 he was elected to the
2 CONT office of InfirmaryDirector and was re-elected in the fall of 1890. He
2 CONT served about eight months on his second term when he sustained the
2 CONT first stroke of paralysis, which induced him to resign. Since then he
2 CONT has sustained four more attacks, the last one resulting in his death."
2 CONT "Mr. Payne has for a great many years been a faithful christian,
2 CONT being an adherent of the Christian church at Shelby. He leaves a wife
2 CONT and four children to mourn their loss. The funeral services will be
2 CONT held from the residence Thursday afternoon, at 2 o'clock, under the
2 CONT auspices of the Shelby I.O.O.F. lodge, of which he was a member."
2 CONT Transcript from the "Shelby Times" published 30 Jan 1892:
2 CONT "Resolutions of Respect by Moreh Encampment No. 170 I.O.O.F.,
2 CONT January 23,
2 CONT 1892."
2 CONT "Whereas, it has pleased the Supreme Architect of the Universe to
2 CONT remove from
2 CONT our midst our beloved patriarch Edwin Payne, therefore be it RESOLVED,
2 CONT that in the death of patriarch Payne, the fraternity has lost one of
2 CONT its truest supporters, a faithful member, the country an exemplary
2 CONT citizen, his surviving wife a devoted and dutiful husband.
2 CONT RESOLVED, that in the life of our deceased patriarch were exemplified
2 CONT in a marked degree the teachings or principles of our honorable
2 CONT institution which serves only as another illustration of the wisdom of
2 CONT the order in selecting such material with which to build up our
2 CONT fraternal.
2 CONT RESOLVED, while we lament his untimely departure and deplore a
2 CONT separation, yet
2 CONT we cherish the hope of a reunion in the Lodge above.
2 CONT RESOLVED, that we tender to the bereaved wife and family our sincere
2 CONT condolence and sympathy in this their hour of sorrow.
2 CONT RESOLVED, that in testimony of our appreciation of patriarch Payne
2 CONT this
2 CONT encampment wear the usual encampment mourning for thirty days.
2 CONT RESOLVED, that these resolutions be spread upon our minutes and copies
2 CONT be furnished to his family and the press for publication.
2 CONT W.H. Houpt,        }
2 CONT Lewis Hines,       } Com.
2 CONT David Hollenbaugh, }
2 CONT P.R. Brickner, Scribe.
2 CONT "Whereas the Great Captain of the Universe has called from our
2 CONT ranks
2 CONT Comrade Edwin Payne, thus again reminding us that so far as "old
2 CONT soldiers" are
2 CONT concerned "this cruel war will soon be over" and that we must all
2 CONT cross the
2 CONT "dead line" into that region where no pensions are awarded, nor
2 CONT attorney fees
2 CONT demanded.
2 CONT RESOLVED, that in the death of Comrade Payne we have suffered the loss
2 CONT of one
2 CONT who was loyal to his flag, and served his country well in time of war;
2 CONT who was
2 CONT true to his friends and served them equally well in time of peace. By
2 CONT those
2 CONT who loved him best, he'll always be remembered; by others - only a
2 CONT little
2 CONT while, - then he, like thousands of others who have gone before, will
2 CONT be forgot. Down deep in the hearts of old friends and comrades, whose
2 CONT sympathies go out to the bereaved family, his memory will long be
2 CONT cherished.
2 CONT RESOLVED, that these resolutions be spread upon and made a part of the
2 CONT minutes of Harker Post No. 146 GAR, also published in city papers and
2 CONT that a copy be sent to the family of the deceased."
2 CONT Harrison Brubaker }
2 CONT S.F. Eckio        }Com.
2 CONT Jno. R. Wolfe     }
