1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Comments to the below:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gray and Warren families are related throughout the years. However, one has to know a little about the entire family, and their history, politics and religious affiliations to determine where his place is.
2 CONT It is very tiresome to have people who have incomplete research writing such dogmatic pronouncements as below. Everyday, more and more research is completing the family links. If you are going to post research could you please pos
2 CONC t the EVIDENCE you are stating or where it can be found. The Warren and Bigelow families moved around not only between the New England colonies, but up to Nova Scotia and Quebec and out to as far a Minnesota at this time. Have you
2 CONC  researched those areas? I think not. We are also relatives of the Mohican, Seneca and Mohawk peoples. Try reading a few more books. The below is most certainly NOT impeccable research! Many Quakers did not "register" their childr
2 CONC en if they were not near a meetinghouse. And you didn't even go to New Hampshire???
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT I did not create this memorial because I do not believe that find-a-grave memorials should be created for people whose deaths and burials are unknown. But I inherited it from another Warren family researcher and can't delete it. S
2 CONC o it exists. .
2 CONT We do not know the birth or death dates or places for Jabez Warren.  Nor do we have the names of his parents.  [This is after 100 years of impeccable research by descendants of this line. There are no birth or death records for Ja
2 CONC bez in''' CT, MA, or VT'''.]  Moreover, DNA research shows that Jabez' descendants carry DNA that is identical with DNA from the descendants of Edward Gray, putting Jabez' paternity in question. .
2 CONT Husband of Mary Bi--, whom he married on Jan. 16, 1717, in Lebanon, New London, CT.  [Unfortunately, the corner of the page in the church record book was torn off about 150 years ago, so we do not have Mary's maiden name.] There i
2 CONC s a lot of conjecture but absolutely no evidence to support the hypothesis that his wife's maiden name was Bishop or Bissell or Bingham. .
2 CONT This couple had 5 known children, David, Nathaniel, Mary, Jabez Jr and Gideon Warren, whose births were recorded at Brimfield, MA, although it is doubtful that they were all born there. .
2 CONT Please do not send me edits for any of the above unless you have discovered a heretofore unknown document or bible record.  Everything else has been thoroughly vetted.  Thank you. .
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/64479306/jabez-warren Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 7 2019, 12:12:24 UTC''
1 FAMS @F6000000018359640881@
1 FAMS @F5400801297770100583@
1 RFN geni:5400801118790100576
1 SUBM @S4510109880520054340@
1 NOTE Jabez was in the military service in the line of forts fromNorthfield, Ma. to the Hoosac during the early French-Indian War, andwas a Corporal at Coleraine, Ma. in 1748.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a `husbandman' in Brimfield, & sold his land there in 1751.
