2 CONC Moosup Valley) Purchase, Scituate, Providence County, RI, Enoch Place bought 300 acres for 1500 Pounds from Stephen & Elizabeth Herrington, of North Kingstown. On 17 Oct 1753 at Scituate, Providence county, RI, Enoch Place sold Th
2 CONC omas Parker 50 acres for 350 Pounds; "southwest corner of my farm"; witnessed by Robert Love and Caleb Greene; wife Hannah also signed. He was admitted free in Scituate in 1754, Providence county, RI. He sold 3 acres for 14 Pounds
2 CONC  to William Tyler; witnessed by Thomas Brown & Caleb Greene on 12 Mar 1754 at Scituate, Providence County, RI. He bought 1-1/2 acres for 12 Pounds from William Tyler of Scituate; witnessed by Thomas Brown & Caleb Greene on 12 Mar 
2 CONC 1754 At Scituate, Providence county, RI. He and Hannah Wilcox sold 1 acre for 36 Pounds to William Tyler Jr; Isaac Blanchard and Thomas Brown on 2 Apr 1773 at Scituate, Providence county, RI.
2 CONT ## (1: "Records of the Colony" He was admitted free on 30 Apr 1725 at North Kingston, RI In Sep 1746 etc, Page: Vol. 4, pg 403 2: Scituate Land Evidence: Vol. 4, pg 57 3: Scituate Land Evidence: Vol. 4, pg 251 4: Records of the Co
2 CONC lony: He was admitted free on 30 Apr 1725 at North Kingston, RI In Sep 1746 etc. Supplement of 1875, pg 48 5: Scituate Land Evidence: Vol 4, pg 242 6: Scituate Land Evidence: Vol 4, pg 241 7: Scituate Land Evidence: Vol. 6, pg 358
