2 CONC n-genealogist-the/image?volumeId=13262&pageName=76&rId=24793741 AmericanAncestors] > In this article (published posthumously), Parsons presents evidence that James Arnold in Vital Record of Rhode Island 'conflated into one the sep
2 CONC arate lists of the births of the children of Thomas3 and Margaret (Stafford) [Place] and those of the children of Thomas2 and Hannah (Cole) Place.'
2 CONT ## North Kingstown Births and Deaths, in Arnold, James N. Vital Record of Rhode Island, 1636–1850: First series, births, marriages and deaths. A family register for the people. (Narragansett Hist. Publ. Co., 1891) 91. PLACE, Sarah
2 CONC , of Thomas and Hannah, [born] May 10, 170_. According to Parsons (see citation for TAG 79:76-81), the original records (after the fire) included: '[burned]h Place was born the 10th Day of May 170[burned]' 'Sarah Place Daughter as
2 CONC  abouesaid born [burned]' It appears that Arnold conflated these records. Parsons interpreted the first record as the birth record of Enoch, mentioned in the will of Thomas2.
