1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Stephen Place''' was born circa March 21, 1735 in North Kingstown, Washington County, Rhode Island, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-94907539 Enoch Place, III] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-5748
2 CONC 1846 Hannah (Wilcox) Place]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34706670557 Martha (Perkins) Place] on March 20, 1768. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34706671083 Hannah Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-
2 CONC 94907040 Brig. Gen. Solomon Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-17067000293 Jeremiah Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-17067576293 Newman Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-17069178293 Mehitable Place]; [https://www.geni.
2 CONC com/profile-126838625 Godfrey Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-17070087293 Martha Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-17077764293 Stephen Place, Jr]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-17078142293 Patience Place]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on August 11, 1817 in Foster, Providence County, Rhode Island, United States and was buried in Place-Battey Cemetery. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Believed to have served in Captain Rose's Company in 1758 and in the Campaign of 1762 (Revolutionary War).
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived where his father had lived in the Moosup Valley.
2 CONT
2 CONT His will, dated 10/20/1849 stated the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT I leave my son Raymond G. 40 acres, south part of my farm and a 5 acre woodlot known as plain lot. Raymond was directed to pay Olive L. Valentine $200.00. Olive and Sarah Ann Vaughn, were also left $400.00 in the will. A Roby A. P
2 CONC lace, was left $200.00 dollars. Son of Enoch Place and his wife Hannah Wilcox. Married Martha Perkins on March 29, 1768.
