1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Enoch Place, Jr.''' was born in 1748. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-94907539 Enoch Place, III] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-57481846 Hannah (Wilcox) Place]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Enoch married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34673811688 Ruth Hammond]. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34673811694 Peleg Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34696896285 Joseph G Place]; [h
2 CONC ttps://www.geni.com/profile-34705164956 George Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34673811693 Betsey Place]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on April 1, 1819 in Foster, Providence County, Rhode Island, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT According to the Muster and Pay Rolls of the War of the Revolution, 1775-1783. Enoch Place had the rank of Sargent Major in the 2nd Rhode Island State Regiment , Colo Archibald Crary's Regiment in the Service of the United States.
2 CONT
