1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''Caution: Not son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Brig-Gen-Solomon-Place/6000000009507476412 Brig. Gen. Solomon Place].''
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Caution: Do not confuse him with the [https://www.geni.com/people/T-Place/6000000220856148833 Thomas Place] who married [https://www.geni.com/people/Eunice-Place/6000000002228953617 Eunice Holden]. That Thomas can be traced in N
2 CONC ew York censuses 1850-1870.''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Thomas Place''' was born in 1803 in Saratoga, Saratoga County, New York, United States. His parents were probably [https://www.geni.com/profile-38906560 Shadrach Place] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-38906310 Susannah]. He w
2 CONC as a Farmer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married [https://www.geni.com/profile-94906563 Eunice (Shaw) Place] in 1829. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * 1830 [https://www.geni.com/profile-94906393 William Thomas Place]; married [https://www.geni.com/profile-94906423 Catherine Elizabeth STOTTS]
2 CONT * 1832 [https://www.geni.com/profile-38904917 Thomas Washington Place]; married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34675403500 Rebecca Jane EASTER]
2 CONT * 1834 [https://www.geni.com/profile-38906549 Amelia Abigail Place]; married [https://www.geni.com/profile-38905907 Alonzo CRAWFORD]
2 CONT * 1837 [https://www.geni.com/profile-34675403807 Abby A. Place]; married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34675405032 Calvin GOODRICH] 
2 CONT * 1839 [https://www.geni.com/profile-38906192 Jerome H Place]; 
2 CONT * 1841 [https://www.geni.com/profile-38905449 Delilah Isabelle Place]; married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34721700086 David MORRISON] 
2 CONT * 1844 [https://www.geni.com/profile-38906225 Daniel Clay Place] married [https://www.geni.com/profile-38905915 Jane Helen BENSON]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34739439169 Irene Ann Adelaide Place]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a farmer. He and his family went to Huron County, Ohio in 1833, when he bought 199 acres of land for $398 (Huron Co. Deed Bk. 7:557). He and his wife Eunice sold 99 acres to his brother Solomon in 1835 for $200 (Huron Co. D
2 CONC eed Bk. 12:393). Thomas and Eunice were living in Ripley Township in 1840, and in Fairfield Township in 1850, when Thomas' property was valued at $4,000.
2 CONT
2 CONT In June 1845 Thomas and his sister-in-law Abigail Place were appointed administrators of the estate of his brother Solomon (Huron Co. Probate Bk., 329).
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on February 26, 1893 in Auburn, Cayuga, New York, USA and was buried circa March 3, 1893 in Old North Fairfield Cemetery (Plot Row 12), North Fairfield, Huron County, Ohio, United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Obituary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of Mr Thomas Place
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Thomas Place, one of the old pioneers of Fairfield township, but who has resided in Auburn, N.Y., during several years past, died at his home last Monday. The remains reached Fairfield Thursday and the funeral was held at the 
2 CONC Congregational church, after which the burial took place in the cemetary near the village.
2 CONT
2 CONT Our Fairfield correspondent says:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Place came to Fairfield as early as 1833 and was for many years one of our most prosperous farmers, and at the same time a successful stock buyer and drover. He has made annual visits to this place during many years past and w
2 CONC as always warmly greeted by his old pioneer friends and acquaintances. He was 89 years old at the time of his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Place was well known in Norwalk, and since leaving Huron county, paid annual visits to his old home. He was a subscriber to the REFLECTOR at the very beginning, and his name has been on our books most of the time for over 63 y
2 CONC ears, being still there at the time of his death. (The Norwalk Reflector, Norwalk, Ohio, March 7, 1893.)
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1850 - Corinth, Saratoga, New York, United States
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1850 - Fairfield, Huron, Ohio, United States
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1855 - Hadley, Saratoga, New York, United States
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1860 - Town of Hadley, Saratoga, New York, United States
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1870 - Ohio, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Corinth, Saratoga, New York, United States - 1850
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Hadley, Saratoga, New York, United States - 1855
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Town of Hadley, Saratoga, New York, United States - 1860
2 CONT * '''Residence''': District 02, Johnsburg, Warren, New York, United States - 1865
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Luzerne, Warren, New York, United States - 1880
2 CONT
2 CONT === Research Notes ===
2 CONT
2 CONT This Thomas Place was not the [https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Place/6000000002228959584 Thomas Place], son of Enoch Place, of Corinth, Saratoga County, New York. That Thomas married Eunice Holden on 7 September 1838. He can be
2 CONC  traced in New York Censuses 1850-1870.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family tradition says this Thomas was a son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Brig-Gen-Solomon-Place/6000000009507476412 Brig. General Solomon Place], but but the evidence does not support the claim. Thomas is not named in Solomon's
2 CONC  family bible or in the administration of Solomon's estate. The relationship is rejected by DAR.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no direct evidence but Thomas was almost certainly a son of Shadrach Place and his wife Susannah, who settled in Cleveland, Ohio.
2 CONT
