1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''Caution: Not son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Brig-Gen-Solomon-Place/6000000009507476412 Brig. Gen. Solomon Place].''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Solomon Place''' was born on January 12, 1811 in NY, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-38906560 Shadrach Place] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-38906310 Susannah]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Solomon married [https://www.geni.com/profile-109263124 Abigail (Shaw) Place] circa 1833 in Fairfield Township, Huron County, Ohio, United States. Together they had the following children: 
2 CONT * 1835 [https://www.geni.com/profile-38906765 Salina Place]. 
2 CONT * 1837 [https://www.geni.com/profile-38905727 Harriet Place]; 
2 CONT * 1840 [https://www.geni.com/profile-38905688 Henrietta Place]; 
2 CONT * 1841 [https://www.geni.com/profile-38905881 Eunice Place]; 
2 CONT * 1844 [https://www.geni.com/profile-38905308 Sarah E Place]; 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on June 10, 1845 in Fairfield, Huron, Ohio, USA, Fairfield Township, Huron County, Ohio, United States and was buried there. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT In 1835 he bought 99 acres in Huron County, Ohio from Thomas and Eunice Place for $200. [Huron Co. Deed Bk. 12:393.]
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in June 1845. His gravestone gives his date of death as 27 August 1845. The administrators for his estate were his widow Abigail and brother Thomas (Huron Co. Probate Bk., 329).
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-211149351-4-3054/solomon-place-in-myheritage-family-trees MyHeritage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 4 2017, 4:04:06 UTC''
