1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DAR# [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_descendants/?action=list&MyPrimary_Seqn=845403&MyLineageCount=1&Control_Min_Seqn=845403 A027134] Private, 4TH Batt. Capt.Jas,Cowden ,Col. James Burd 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Old Presbyterian Church records in Middletown, Dauphin County, Pennsylvania were kept by William Augustus Crabb.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Augustus Crabb and his brother Thomas Crabb who came from Falmouth, Cornwall County, England via their own privately owned ship with a stop in Ireland then to America and settled in Harrisburg and Middletown, Dauphin Count
2 CONC y (then part of Lancaster County), Pennsylvania just prior to the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Crabb owned many houses and much property in Harrisburg and Middletown, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the "Chronicles of Middletown, " C. H. Hutchinson, in 1906 wrote in great details much of the town's history. For instance, the Presbyterian graveyard passed through many owners, including, on June 7, 1802, WILLIAM CRABB, among
2 CONC  others (page 18, C. of M). He further writes, in 1906,..."We have no data, however, respecting any church organization prior to 1850. The records are lost, having been probably been among the private papers of some one of the ori
2 CONC ginal members, who are all dead."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Additional informaion''' [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=crabbe1450&id=I118 Rootsweb]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Augustus Crabb moved his brother Thomas Crabb and family from Hagerstown, Maryland back to Middletown,Pennsylvania when Thomas became ill. [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=crabbe1450&id=I132 Roots
2 CONC web]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Name: William Augustus CRABB
2 CONT * Surname: CRABB
2 CONT * Given Name: William Augustus
2 CONT * Sex: M
2 CONT * Birth: 2 Oct 1743 in Falmouth,Cornwall,England
2 CONT * Christening: 2 Oct 1743 Falmouth,Cornwall,England
2 CONT * Death: 12 Apr 1812 in Middletown,Dauphin,Pennsylvania,USA
2 CONT * Burial: Apr 1812 Old Presbyterian Graveyard, Middletown,Dauphin, Pennsylvania,USA
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.com/books?id=i-NMAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA350&lpg=PA350&dq=kendig+of+swatara&source=bl&ots=BhnCCMhAH_&sig=WjMKbj0FG0xtgOtNNHcGjGIwIDs&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiE9dfxupfMAhXJWj4KHWPQBesQ6AEISDAE#v=onepage&q=kendig&f=false P
2 CONC ennsylvania Genealogy] 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://search.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/sse.dll?indiv=1&db=SARMemberApps&h=557148&tid=28431961&pid=12042748924&usePUB=true&usePUBJs=true&rhSource=2451 Sons of the American Revolution]. William enlisted in 1776 in the 4th Lancaster Cou
2 CONC nty, Pennsylvania regiment under Colonel James Burd. 
