1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Jabez Warren Jr. Mother: Susannah Walker[1]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathan Warren was born in 1757. He was the son of Jabez & Susannah (Walker) Warren. He married Persis Sumner and they had eight known children. They were: Persis, Ithamar, Walter, Ebenezer, Nathan, Orrin, Horace & Harriet. Accordi
2 CONC ng to "A History of the town of Orwell" by Doris Bishop, the family were Baptist. During the war of 1812, Nathan Sr. was in the battle of Plattsburgh, also known as the Battle of Lake Champlain. According to his wife in her applic
2 CONC ation for a pension, she states that four of her sons were in the same battle; Ithamar, Walter, Nathan Jr. & Orrin.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT It is uncertain whether Nathan Warren is buried in this cemetery, but some researchers have his burial here. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in 1757, probably March 29, to Jabez Warren II and Susanna Walker, the middle of 3 known children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In August of 1783 he married Persis Sumner, and they had 8 known children: Persis, Ithamer, Walter, Ebenezer, Nathan Jr., Orrin, Horace & Harriet.  According to "A History of the Town of Orwell, VT" by Doris Bishop, the family was
2 CONC  Baptist. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the War of 1812, Nathan Sr. was in the Battle of Plattsburgh, NY, on Sep. 11, 1814 (also known as the Battle of Lake Champlain).  His wife states in her widow's pension application that 4 of their sons were in the same batt
2 CONC le: Ithamer, Walter, Nathan Jr. & Orrin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some researchers list Nathan Sr.'s dod as 1847, but that is Nathan Jr.  Persis says in the widow's pension application that her husband died in 1827.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21836671/nathan-warren Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 7 2019, 12:47:55 UTC''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Warren-9267
