1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Despite being orphaned before the age of 5, Rebecca Bishop Bigelow lived to be at least 76 years old and had a large, prosperous family. At age 25, she married Ebenezer Bigelow in Chesterfield, Cheshire, New Hampsh
2 CONC ire. By 1802, when Elijah is born in Vermont, they have moved from New Hampshire. When her children moved to Ashford, Cattaraugus, New York she moved with them and is found in the household of her son, Rev. Elijah Bigelow in 1850.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachael was 4 years old when her father died fighting in the Revolutionary War. Her father was born at Chesterfield, New Hampshire and took the oath standing next to John Bishop, who may have been his brother or other kinsman. Joh
2 CONC n was also from Chesterfield. Rachel marries Ebenezer Bigelow Jan. 11, 1798, at Chesterfield, NH. She and Ebenezer lived in Chesterfield, NH until sometime between 1800-1802, they move to Brookline, Windham County, Vermont. They a
2 CONC re enumerated living with Ebenezer's parents (assumed by ages on Vermont census) in 1810. The first two children were born in Chesterfield, NH and the next child was born at Brookline, Windham Co. Ebenezer died in 1845 in Brooklin
2 CONC e, Windham, Vermont. Rachel probably left then to move to Ashford, Cattaraugus Co., New York to be with her sons families.
2 CONT
2 CONT "New Hampshire Birth Records, Early to 1900," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FL2J-5HB : accessed 22 January 2016), Nathan Bishop in entry for Rachel Bishop, 03 Jan 1773; citing Chesterf
2 CONC ield,Cheshire, New Hampshire, United States, Bureau of Vital Records and Health Statistics, Concord; FHL microfilm 1,000,372.
2 CONT
2 CONT "New Hampshire Marriage Records, 1637-1947," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FL8B-LJ9 : accessed 24 January 2016), Ebenezer Bigelow and Rachel Bishop, 11 Jan 1798; citing , , New Hampshi
2 CONC re, Bureau of Vital Records and Health Statistics, Concord; FHL microfilm 1,000,964. Married at Chesterfield, NH Jan. 11, 1798.
2 CONT
2 CONT Still alive in 1850:
2 CONT
2 CONT "United States Census, 1850," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:MCTK-FKZ : accessed 19 March 2016), Rachael Bigelow in household of Elijah Bigelow, Ashford, Cattaraugus, New York, United S
2 CONC tates; citing family 30, NARA microfilm publication M432 (Washington, D.C.: National Archives and Records Administration, n.d.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogy of the Bigelow Family of America: From the Marriage in 1642 of John Biglo and Mary Warren to the Year 1890
2 CONT   Gilman Bigelow Howe 
2 CONT  - January 1, 1890 
2 CONT  C. Hamilton
2 CONT  - Publisher 
2 CONT  Page 446
2 CONT
2 CONT From LDS Records: Rachel Bishop Born Jan. 3, 1773  b. Chesterfield, Chesire, New Hampshire Married to Ebenezer Bigelow Jan. 11, 1798 _____________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT From Bigelow Family website: Rachel Bishop  ‎(I19230)‎ 15336.1     Ebenezer 6 BIGELOW, son of Paul 5 ( Cornelius 4( Samuel 3, Samuel 2, John 1) and Hannah (OBER) BIGELOW, was born 18 Oct 1762 at Upton, Westborough county, MA. The 
2 CONC family removed to Windlam county, VT at the close of the Revolutionary War. '''About 1795 Ebenezer married Rachel Bishop of''' '''NH''' and they lived a few years at Chesterfield, Cheshire co, New Hampshire (then New York), but ci
2 CONC rca 1801 returned to Vermont and settled at Brookline, Windham county. Ebenezer was died in June 1845. . His wife Rachel moved with some of their family to Ashford, Cattaraugus county, NY, and was living 1850, but deceased before 
2 CONC 1860. She was born circa 1775, estimating from census.  Rachel is most probably buried at the Bond Cemetery in Ashford, N. Y.  Children of Ebenezer and Rachel (Bishop) Bigelow: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15336.11     Betsy, b ca 1796 NH. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15336.12t    Mary (called Polly), b ca 1798 NH; d 22 Sep 1834 Ashford, NY; m 24 Nov 1816 Daniel Mansfield Cole. 9 children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15336.13t    Nancy, b ca 1800 Chesterfield, NH; d 23 May 1838 Ashford, NY; m 26 Dec 1835 Daniel M Cole, her sister's widower. 1 son. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15336.14t    Elijah (Rev.), b 16 Nov 1802 Brookline, Windham co, VT; d 25 May 1876 Ashford, Cattaraugus co, NY; m 15 Nov 1827 Rebecca Johnson; res Ashford, NY. 9 children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15336.15     Susan, b ca 1804 Brookline, VT. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15336.16     Hannan, b ca 1806 Brookline, VT. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15336.17t    Ezra, b 31 Mar 1808 Brookline, VT; d 10 July 1891 (buried Ashford, NY); m Calista Andrews; res Springville and Ashford, NY. 9 children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15336.18     Phebe, b ca 1810 Brookline, VT; m (between 1827-1832) Josephus Slate. 1 son. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 15336.19     Laura, b ca 181 Brookline, VT; d ____
2 CONT  ; m 10 Apr 1833 Levi Johnson.  Sources: 
2 CONT  Bigelow Society,The Bigelow Family Genealogy Vol I, pg 238; 
2 CONT  Howe, Bigelow Family of America; 
2 CONT  censuses l790-l870 NH, VT, NY; 
2 CONT  cemetery inscriptions, Ashford, NY; 
2 CONT  vital records VT; 
2 CONT  history Cattaraugus co, NY; 
2 CONT  correspondence with descendants. 
