2 CONT Mrs. William N. Dunsmore of Los Angeles, CA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the war his service included: Rapidan Campaign 4 May - 12 Jun 1864; Totopotomoy May 28-31. Cold Harbor June 1-12. Siege of Petersburg 17 Jun 1864, to 2 Apr 1865. Jerusalem Plank Road 22 Jun 1864. Fort Fisher, Petersburg, 25
2 CONC  Mar 1865. Appomattox Campaign 28 Mar - 9 Apr 1865. Assaults on and fall of Petersburg 2 Apr 1865. Sailor's Creek 6 Apr 1986. Appomattox Court House 9 Apr 1865 for the surrender of Lee and his army. After the war, Solon took up fa
2 CONC rming in the Wellsboro area.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/89117475/solon-l_-warren
2 CONT
