1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/38331498/delano-emerson-warren
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo by Laurie Stewart Tokarsky
2 CONT
2 CONT Age 20 years
2 CONT
2 CONT Delano was the son of Lucius Platt Warren and Melissa Reynolds. He was a great grandson of Col. Gideon Warren who fought in the Revolutionary war with Ethan Allen, and was injured at Fort Ticonderoga.
2 CONT
2 CONT Delano Emerson Warren enlisted as a private in Co. C of the 183rd Regiment of the NY State Voluntary Infantry at Dunkirk, NY. This regiment was shortly after absorbed into Co. A, 188th Regiment NYSV. His enlistment papers describe
2 CONC  Delano as a young man of 18 years, 5' 9" tall, blue eyes, light hair and light complexion, occupation: mechanic. Delano fought at the Battle at Hatcher's Run in VA on October 27, 1864. It was the first battle for his regiment and
2 CONC  seven weeks after his enlistment. During his war service, Delano contracted TB. Though he spent many months at army hospitals in Washington, D.C.; West Philadelphia, PA; Annapolis and Baltimore, MD, Delano never recovered. He was
2 CONC  mustered out, an invalid, on June 10, 1865 at Elmira, NY and died at home one year later of incipient tuberculosis. He never married.
