2 CONT National Archives Nathan Hills
2 CONT Sent to Nathan R. Hills in response to inquire by George Hills and Nathan R. Hills
2 CONT for Pension or bounty lands due Dec'd Nathan Hills. From  Connecticut Pension office Washington DC. May 1851 " The declaration in the case of Nathan Hills, Dec'd is totally irragular and defective."
2 CONT Sent to Hulda De Long Watertown, N Y, 1906 
2 CONT Nathan Hills a Private in Captain Bernard's Conn. company. Enlisted Feb 12 1778
2 CONT Promoted carpal Sept 1st in third Regiment Connecticut line Formation, 1777-1781,Colomal Samuel Wyllis. On Page 321 same book appears the following-
2 CONT Carpal Nathan Hills paid from Jan 1st 1781 to Dec 31 1781, in Capt John Durkees Conn Army in First regiment Conn line formation 1781 to 1783.Colonel John Durkee- Officers of Company from Norwich, Windham and Dunstable Mass. signed
2 CONC  by Wm E. F. Landers ,Col asst Adjutant General.
2 CONT From History of Washington Co, NY 1737 - 1878 by Everts and Ensign, 1878 Page 404: "Nathan Hills came from Hartford, CT about 1793 and lived in the town of Hartford, Washington Co, where he was a farmer. He had nine children, Will
2 CONC  of "Nathan Hills of Hartford Dated Sept. 4,1811 Probated Dec. 29, 1811 Mentions: wife,Jerusha dau:Hannah, Cynthia, Sarah, Anna and Huldah sons:Nathan, George, Samuel and David
2 CONT
2 CONT With greatful thanks to John Butzke  for the
