1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 10. Chester WEBSTER was born on 17 Mar 1785 in Gill, Franklin,  Massachusetts.86,87,88 He was baptised on 15 Feb 1786.89 He Int. Marriage  on 9 Aug 1805 in Gill, Franklin, Massachusetts.90 He died on 8 Aug 1864 in 
2 CONC  Hampden, Geauga, Ohio.91,92 History and Genealogy of the Gov. John Webster  Family of Connecticut, by William Holcomb Webster and Rev. Melville Reuben  Webster, 1st Edition; Published by Andrews Printing Co., 1915. p. 410
2 CONT  A farmer and cooper, remained at Gill, Mass., and with his brother Price,  carried on his father's old farm until after 1807, and then removed to  Canton, St. Lawrence, New York. He is said to have gone from there to Upper  Canad
2 CONC a, near Niagara Falls, and it is thought that some of his descendants  may be living now near Suspension Bridge or Niagara Falls in Canada, as they  were traced there 25 years ago.
2 CONT  Chester Webster enlisted in the War of 1812, in the New York Militia, at  Canton, N. Y., and served at or near Ogdensburgy, N. Y., from the 10th to the  19th of Sept., 1812. On the 28th of April 1859, he was residing at Hampden, 
2 CONC  Geauga County, Ohio, where he died August 8, 1864.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Asenath (Senney) WRISLEY (daughter of Asahel RISLEY and  Darcas PETTEE) on 8 Sep 1805 in Gill, Franklin, Massachusetts.93,94,95  Asenath (Senney) WRISLEY was born about 1785 in Greenfield, Franklin,  Massachusett
2 CONC s.96 She died on 29 Oct 1856 in Hampden, Geauga, Ohio.97,98  Chester WEBSTER and Asenath (Senney) WRISLEY had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT +43 i. Louisa WEBSTER.
2 CONT  +44 ii. Hiram WEBSTER.
2 CONT  +45 iii. Melinda WEBSTER.
2 CONT  46 iv. George WEBSTER was born on 1 Aug 1811 in , Ontario, Canada.99,100  History of the Town of Gill, Massachusetts. Volume IV, Genealogies J-Z by  Ralph M. Stoughton, 1960.
2 CONT  Disappeared while the family lived in Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT History and Genealogy of the Gov. John Webster Family of  Connecticut, by William Holcomb Webster and Rev. Melville Reuben Webster, 1st  Edition; Published by Andrews Printing Co., 1915.
2 CONT  George left home when they lived in Canada. Never heard of him  again (Miss Harriet M. Gardiner.)
2 CONT  +47 v. Harriet WEBSTER. http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/WEBSTER/1999-12/0945556280
