1 NAME Sarah E. /Haviland/
2 GIVN Sarah E.
2 SURN Haviland
2 _MARNM Webster
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Ithaca City Cemetery, Ithaca, Tompkins County, New York, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 26 DEC 1811
2 PLAC Patterson, Putnam, New York, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 OCT 1885
2 PLAC Evanston, Cook, Illinois, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (Chicago Tribune; Chicago, IL.  Tuesday, October 20, 1885, page 8.)
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATHS.
2 CONT
2 CONT WEBSTER – At Evanston, Sabbath evening, Oct. 18, Mrs. Sarah E. Webster, aged 73 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services at the residence of her son, T.K. Webster, No. 303 Maple av., Tuesday at 4 p.m.  Friends can take the 3 o’clock train from N.W.R.R. depot.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT (Ithaca Daily Journal; Ithaca, NY.  Friday, October 23, 1885, page 3.)
2 CONT
2 CONT DR. WEBSTER’S RELICT BURIED IN ITHACA.
2 CONT
2 CONT The bringing to Ithaca and interring in the old cemetery here of the mortal remains of the relict of the late Dr. H.K. Webster, is an event of melancholy interest to older residents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Webster, thirty-five years ago, was a practicing physician here.  He enjoyed a high standing in his profession, for his skill and success were great and he was universally esteemed.  Prior to his active practice he owned and c
2 CONC onducted the West End drug store, of which Hasting & Todd are the present proprietors.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of his death in April 1857 Dr. Webster owned the residence subsequently purchased by Mr. Leonard Treman of the widow, and now occupied by him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eighteen years ago Mrs. Webster removed to Evanston, Ill., a large suburban town but eleven miles from Chicago.  Here she quietly lived until Sunday last, the twentieth instant, when she quickly passed away, at the advanced age of
2 CONC  seventy-three, of neuralgia of the heart.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her son, Mr. Towner K. Webster, brought her remains to Ithaca and on Tuesday morning they were laid by the side of her long sleeping husband.  Mr. Webster is engaged in business in Chicago, and had visited this locality, in accord
2 CONC ance with his annual custom, bringing then his wife to enjoy with him a view of his old home scenery which he pronounces the most beautiful in the country which he has traveled extensively.  The relict of Dr. Webster had been a li
2 CONC fe long member of the Baptist denomination but owing to a conflicting engagement of the pastor of that church, the Rev. Mr. Munger kindly read the solemn service of the dead at the grave.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/39388533/sarah-eliza-webster Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 27 2023, 18:09:01 UTC''
