2 CONT Towner Keeney Webster
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT 31 July 1849
2 CONT in Ithaca, Tompkins County, New York
2 CONT Death
2 CONT 11 October 1922
2 CONT in Evanston, Cook County, Illinois 
2 CONT
2 CONT      WEBSTER, TOWNER KEENEY.— Born in Ithaca, New York, July 31, 1849. Son of H.K. and S.E. Webster, who were descended from early American ancestors. Mr. Webster was educated in a common school, and at the age of twelve years was
2 CONC  employed as a clerk in a country store. He came to Chicago in February, 1867, and for several years was engaged in merchandising. In 1876 he comnenced in a modest way, and with very little capital, the manufacturing business, whi
2 CONC ch has since grown to such immense proportions under his supervision and direction. He is the founder and president of the Webster Manufacturing Company, engineers,founders and machinists, which was established fifteen years ago i
2 CONC n a one-story wooden building about 15 x 30 feet in area, with a working force of Mr. Webster and one other man. The plant now occupies two and a quarter acres at Western avenue and Fifteenth street, covered by substantial brick b
2 CONC uildings with an aggregate floor space under one roof amounting to 120,504 square feet, wherein are emploved about 600 men, Mr. Webster is a republican, a member of the Union League Club, and is actively connected with the Presbyt
2 CONC erian church. He was married July 7, 1874, to Emma Josephine Kitchell, and has four sons and two daughters. His home is in Evanston. -  The hand-book of Chicago biography: a compendium of useful biographical information for refere
2 CONC nce and study, John Joseph Flinn, Publisher,The Standard guide, 1893.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/59882896/towner-keeney-webster Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCop
