1 NAME Henry Augustus /Russell/
2 GIVN Henry Augustus
2 SURN Russell
2 _MARNM Russell
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Riverside Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Riceville
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE AUG 1858
2 ADDR
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 MAR 1935
2 ADDR
3 CITY Riceville
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry Augustus Russell 1858-1935
2 CONT
2 CONT #1 RUSSELL RITES WILL BE FRIDAY RICEVILLE MAN, INJURED IN FALL, LEAVES WIDOW AND TWO SONS
2 CONT
2 CONT Riceville, March 6 – Funeral services for Augustus Russell who fell on the street, causing concussion of the brain, are to be held Friday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Besides his widow, he is survived by two sons, Frank and Clifford who are on their way here from California.  Another son, Eddie, preceded him in death many years ago, as a result of being mangled by a traveling bear on exhibition
2 CONC  here.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Russell is survived by a niece, Mrs. Helen Leffler of Livermore, who came to be with her aunt at this time.  A nephew, Earl Hughes of Chicago also survives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon the death of his twin sister, Mr. Russell took this niece and nephew into his home and cared for them through their high school days.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mason City Globe Gazette, Wednesday, March 6, 1935
2 CONT
2 CONT #2 Henry Augustus Russell was born August 1858 in Iowa (1900 Census) , the son of Elias and Charlotte (Cole) Russell (1925 Iowa Census) .  He married Clara Idalia Warren, the daughter of Abel Fayette Warren and Martha (Albright) W
2 CONC arren Fassett. The niece and nephew mentioned in the obit were the children of his sister Lucy Alinda Russell and James Thomas Hughes.
2 CONT
2 CONT #3  South Dakota Births:1856-1903 for their son Clifford Name: Clifford Augustus Russell  Birth Date: 9 Nov 1883  Gender: Male  County: Clark  Father's Name: Henry Augustus Russell  Mother's name: Clara Idalia Warren
