1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Thomas Place, Sr.''' was born circa 1663 in North Kingstown, Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-57432896 Enoch Place, Sr.] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-5743289
2 CONC 7 Sarah (...) Place]. He was a Recorder of York. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married [https://www.geni.com/profile-22050318 Hannah (Cole) Place] in 1694 in Boston, Suffolk Co., MA. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-50899555 Mary (Place) Kenyon]; [https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/profile-28475048 John Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-28475002 Marbury (Place) Stafford]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-22050262 Thomas Place, Jr.]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-28475105 Joseph Place]; [https://www.ge
2 CONC ni.com/profile-28475080 Sarah Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-94907539 Enoch Place, III]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-50900694 Samuel Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-28475126 Ann Place]; [https://www.geni.com/profile
2 CONC -50799024 Unknown Place]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on November 27, 1727 in North Kingstown, Kings County, Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Austin Genealogical Dictionary of Rhode Island provides the following information regarding the family of Thomas Place: Thomas Place married Hannah (Cole) Place (1668-1734), daughter of John & Susanna (Hutchinson) Cole; [4] Thomas
2 CONC  and Hannah were the parents of the following children: [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mary; 5 Jan 169_.
2 CONT # Marbury; 5 May 169_
2 CONT # Thomas, 2 Nov 169_.
2 CONT # John, 24 April 170_.
2 CONT # Sarah; 10 May 170_
2 CONT # Joseph; 22 Dec 170_
2 CONT # Samuel, Sep 170_
2 CONT # Enoch
2 CONT # Ann
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT *'''COLE, Hannah 
2 CONT *d. ABT 1734 North Kingston, Washington, RI.
