2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Tiffany-38
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Will
2 CONT
2 CONT From THE TIFFANYS OF AMERICA HISTORY AND GENEALOGY : [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT  In the name of God Amen ; the twentieth-eighth day of June 1732. 
2 CONT
2 CONT James Tifiny of the Town of Attleborough in the County of Bristol in his Majesties province of the Massachusetts Bay ; being very sick and weak in body but of perfect mind and memory thanks to be given to god therefor, calling to 
2 CONC mind the mortality of my body and knowing that it is appointed for all men once to dye ; do make and ordain this my last will and Testament. 
2 CONT
2 CONT That is to say principally and first of all I give and Recommend my soul into the hands of god that gave it and my body I recommend to the earth to be buried in decent “Christian Burial" at the discretion of my executors: Nothing 
2 CONC doubting but at the General Resurrection I 'hall receive the same again by the mighty power of god. 
2 CONT
2 CONT And as touching such worldly estate wherewith it hath pleased god to bless me in this life, I give demise and dispose in the "followin" manner and form. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Imprimis : I give and bequeath to Elizabeth my dearly beloved wife, accordin as the laws of our province hath provided that is to say the income of the third part of my estate : together with the use of any Room in my dwelling hou
2 CONC se. 
2 CONT
2 CONT And I do constitute make and ordain Elizabeth my dearly beloved wife together with my Son John Tifinye both joyntly to be executrix and executor of this my last will and Testament. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give to my well beloved son Joseph "Tifinie" ten Shillings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give to my well beloved Son James Tifinye the sum of ten shillings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give unto my well beloved son Samuel Tifinie the sum of ten shillings : the Reason why I give unto these my Sons no more of my estate now is "becaus" they had the greater part of their portion before. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give unto my well beloved Son Benjamin " Tifinye " A hundred Acres of land in Ashford in the Colony of Connecticut 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give unto my daughter Elizabeth's Children the sum of five pound six Shillings and eight pence 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give onto my well beloved daughter Anne the sum of four pounds 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give unto my well beloved daughter Rebecca, the sum of six pounds 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give onto my well beloved daughter Sarah the sum of six pounds 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give unto my well beloved daughter Mary the sum of six pounds 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give unto my well beloved daughter Martha the sum of five pounds 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give unto my well beloved daughter "Lidia" the sum of three pounds 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give unto my well beloved daughter Bathsheba the sum of five pounds 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I do hereby give unto my well beloved sons John Tifinye and Noah Tifinye all my estate equal for quantity and quality for them to enjoy forever 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give unto my daughters Kesiah and Aletheah the sum of thirty pounds each of them, obliging my two younger sons to pay out all their Legacy's “att” the term of yean when my youngest son is three and twenty years old. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I do hereby utterly disallow revoke and disannull all and every other former testament wills Legacies and bequests and exetors "be" me in any ways before named willed and bequeathed Ratifying and confirming this and no other to be
2 CONC  my last will and testament in witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal the day and year Above, sd 
2 CONT
2 CONT JAMES TIFFANY Seal 
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Sealed published pronounced and declared to be my last Will and testament in the presence of us the Subscribers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ephraim Lane 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Lane 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Fuller 
2 CONT
2 CONT Proved July 26th, 1732. 
2 CONT
