2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Tiffany-35 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 12 2017, 2:30:15 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth 	1 Sep 1710 Attleboro, Bristol County, Massachusetts, USA Death 	10 Jan 1788 (aged 77) Attleboro, Bristol County, Massachusetts, USA Burial 	 Old Kirk Yard Attleboro, Bristol County, Massachusetts, USA Memorial ID 	67807900 
2 CONT Died in the 78th year of his age.
2 CONT
2 CONT John, the son of James Tiffany (1666-1732) and Bethiah Fuller (1670-1711), married Deliverance Parmenter (1717-1798) on 26 May 1737. John and Deliverance Tiffany had twelve children. Their four daughters were Esther, Deliverance, 
2 CONC Martha, and Ann. 
2 CONT Their eight sons were John, Humphrey, Noah, Hosea, Thomas, Abijah, Zechariah, and Hezekiah. 
2 CONT Hezekiah is buried at Bushnell Cemetery in Sodus, Wayne County, New York (Find A Grave Memorial# 23114722).
2 CONT "The family in Susquehanna county are the descendants of John and Deliverance (Parmenter) Tiffany, prominent settlers at Attleboro, Mass., where they lived and died. 
2 CONT They reared a family of sons and daughters who were inspired with patriotism, devotion, and aggressive achievement. 
2 CONT The sons all served in the Revolutionary war, and became noted pioneers in the spread of civilization westward from New England centers. 
2 CONT The daughters became noble pioneer women. John Tiffany died at Attleboro in 1788. 
2 CONT His wife, who was born in 1718, died in 1798. 
2 CONT Their sons were Capt. John, Zachariah, Ezra, Noah, Hosea and Thomas; their daughters were Patty, Esther and Anna." (from the book "Northeastern Pennsylvania.")
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/67807900/john-tiffany
2 CONT
