2 CONC h patriotism, devotion, and aggressive achievement. The sons all served in the Revolutionary war, and became noted pioneers in the spread of civilization westward from New England centers. The daughters became noble pioneer women.
2 CONC  John Tiffany died at Attleboro in 1788. His wife, who was born in 1718, died in 1798. Their sons were Capt. John, Zachariah, Ezra, Noah, Hosea and Thomas; their daughters were Patty, Esther and Anna." (from the book "Northeastern
