1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''William Thomas Place''' was born on July 21, 1830 in New York, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-94906514 Thomas Place] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-94906563 Eunice (Shaw) Place]. He was a Retai
2 CONC l Grocer and Farmer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William married [https://www.geni.com/profile-94906423 Catherine Elizabeth (Stotts) Place] on 23 October 1853 Huron County, Ohio. Together they had the following children: 
2 CONT * 1855 [https://www.geni.com/profile-94906177 George Washington Place]; married https://www.geni.com/people/Jane-Place/6000000009506826060 and https://www.geni.com/people/Albertina-Place/6000000033840246885
2 CONT * 1857 [https://www.geni.com/profile-38905466 Francis Place]. died young
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on July 26, 1882 in Ogemaw Township, Ogemaw County, Michigan, United States and was buried in 1882 in Brookside Cemetery, West Branch, Ogemaw County, Michigan, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT He was a farmer and a retail grocer. He marriage license shows his middle initial as S. Other records show T. In 1860 he and his wife were living in Greenwich, Huron County, Ohio, where he was a farmer with $3,000 in real estate a
2 CONC nd $100 in personal property. They had a servant Mary York. On 23 May 1863 he was appointed guardian of his wife's niece Mary Ann Stotts, daughter of her brother John. On 10 September 1863 he filed a petition to sell her part of t
2 CONC he inheritance, and the petition was opposed by Mary Ann's step- mother Catherine (Walling) Stotts.
2 CONT
2 CONT William and his family moved to Ogemaw County, Michigan about 1878, and were among the pioneer families of that area. The 1880 census shows him as a retail grocer. He employed one servant, Nellie Potter (age 16, born in New York t
2 CONC o English parents).
2 CONT
2 CONT William T. and Catharin E. Place homesteaded 160 acres in Ogemaw County, Michigan on 25 February 1890.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1850 - Fairfield, Huron, Ohio
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1860 - Greenwich Township, Huron, Ohio, United States
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1870 - Ohio, United States
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1880 - Klacking, Ogemaw, Michigan, United States
2 CONT
