2 CONC ge 61, a millwright by occupation, died of consumption. The mortality information would indicate his death in December 1849 rather than 1850.
2 CONT
2 CONT His birth has been reported as 1780 Cumberland County on DAR applications, but based on mortality schedule, would be c.1778.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pennsylvania Marriages on familysearch gives a transcription of Planket Crab marriage to Catharine Jungster on Nov 7, 1816, with source of First Evangelical Lutheran Church records, Carlisle, PA. (document not viewable for confirm
2 CONC ation of transcription).
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1850 census for Monroe Township shows a Catharine Crab as head of household with Amelia 15, Elizabeth 19, Josephine 13, Margaret 11, and Henry A 9.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harrisburg Telegraph, Harrisburg, PA, 6 May 1899: TOMBSTONE RECORDS From Town Graveyard, Carlisle, of Persons Born Prior to 1800. Crabb, Plunkett A., b. 1788; d. 1850
2 CONT
2 CONT Carlisle Weekly Herald, Carlisle, Pa 02 Jan 1850, Wed pg 2 DIED At Silver Spring Forge on the 19th ult after a long and severe illness, PLUNKET A CRABB, in the 60th year of his age.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Plunkett Augustus Crabbe served as a Private under Captain Walker, Colonel Kennedy in the 1st Regiment, 1st Brigade PA Militia from August 29, 1814 until March 5, 1815.
