1 NOTE {geni:about_me} At the age of 17, he entered the printing office of Simon Cameron, at Harrisburg, where he acquired the knowledge of the art preservative. In 1865 he started the Democratic State Journal, which he edited with abili
2 CONC ty. In 1848 he was the editor of The Commonwealth, which had but a brief existence, and in that same year, The Argus, in connection with Valentine Best, who was proprietor of the paper. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1852 he took a position in Harrisburg, at the Patriot, which he edited with much vigor. As a journalist, he ranked with the ablest writers of the day.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=i-NMAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA350&lpg=PA350&dq=kendi
