1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Henry Crabb born 1640, transported to MD April 1665 by James Bringle who received a 200 A grant. Worked until 1672 to pay transport.  Two sons: Ralph, born 1670 and Thomas born 1665 (Col. Thomas Crabbe).   Col. Thomas Crabb died i
2 CONC n 1719 Charles County, MD.  He married Elizabeth.  Named plantation Wiltshire.  They may be from Wiltshire (Shire) England.
2 CONT Edward III consulted with Crabbe of Walton, pilot, before the Battle of Crecy, 1346
