1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for NEW YORK with the rank of PRIVATE.
2 CONT [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A079189  DAR Ancestor # A079189]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT An excerpt taken from footnotes contained in the book THE BENONI MOON FAMILY written by W. Fred Wickizer.  Admittedly, this is not definitive... "3 Over 50 years, some family historians surmised that Benoni was most likely a son o
2 CONC f either Peleg 4 or
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Moon. Researchers asserting the parentage as Peleg, approximated Benoni’s birth date as between
2 CONT
2 CONT 1752-1755. Consequently, since Peleg and Sarah (Baxter) Moon were married in Newport, RI on
2 CONT
2 CONT November 6, 1751, then it was thought that Benoni was likely their child. Additionally, Peleg’s daughter,
2 CONT
2 CONT Esther Moon married a John Brown, Jr. This John Brown, Jr. with Benoni Moon purchased property in
2 CONT
2 CONT North Stephentown, NY, seemingly showing a close connection between Benoni and Peleg’s family. Since
2 CONT
2 CONT Benoni owned property (Little Hoosick farms) near both Peleg and Robert’s children, it is difficult to say
2 CONT
2 CONT whether his farm locations are suggestive of any particular relationship. By about March 1779 (see
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephentown, NY tax list), Peleg moved from Exeter, RI to the Mattison Hollow area near Cherry Plaines and
2 CONT
2 CONT Berlin, NY (then known as Stephentown, NY) with several of his children. Nearby in Berlin, NY were
2 CONT
2 CONT several sons and daughters of Robert and Ann (Tripp) Moon, including Mehitable, Job (b.1739/40), John
2 CONT
2 CONT R. (b. cir 1741), and Deliverance (b. May 13,1736) all of whom attended the 7th Day Baptist Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, Benoni is not recorded as attending this Church or any Church in Stephentown. However,
2 CONT
2 CONT Benoni also owned property (roaring brook farm) in North Stephentown, NY near John5 Moon (not to be
2 CONT
2 CONT confused with John R. Moon) and wife Ruth. In fact, John and Ruth are buried in a small cemetery know
2 CONT
2 CONT as Moon cemetery on Benoni’s original farm. Peleg Moon is buried on the farm of his son, Thomas in the
2 CONT
2 CONT Mattison Hollow area. On May 11, 1782, Peleg with his two sons Thomas and Benajah, as well as his son
2 CONT
2 CONT in law, Jonathan Brown and other neighbors, were sworn in by local officials to defend the New York
2 CONT
2 CONT frontiers. Benoni was not included in this list, but does appear on the on the 4th and 6th Albany Militia lists.
2 CONT
2 CONT Researchers maintaining Benoni’s paternal parentage as being Robert4 Moon were frustrated by North
2 CONT
2 CONT Kingstown, R.I’s. courthouse fires that partially destroyed the name and birth dates of Robert and Ann
2 CONT
2 CONT (Tripp) Moon’s children, including Benoni’s name and birth date. From about 1990 to 1999, Dr. Tom
2 CONT
2 CONT Clark asserted that the pattern of names in Benoni’s family are closely associated with Robert4 rather than
2 CONT
2 CONT Peleg4 Moon’s family and outweigh other circumstantial factors (in favor of Peleg). For example, Benoni named his first son Robert, likely after his father. Also, Ann Tripp, Benoni’s alleged mother, has a brother,
2 CONT
2 CONT Benoni Tripp. Presumably, she named Benoni after this brother. Additionally, Ann has a brother Job and a
2 CONT
2 CONT sister Mehitable. Robert also has a sister Mehitable. These names are also repeated among Robert and
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann (Tripp) Moon’s grand children. However, Wendell Eby located the strongest piece of evidence
2 CONT
2 CONT pointing towards Robert Moon being the father of Benoni. This evidence consisted of a photograph of
2 CONT
2 CONT Wanton Moon (b. 1800, Benoni’s youngest child) identifying the date of his father’s birth date as April 12,
2 CONT
2 CONT 1745. Obviously, since Peleg and Sarah married in 1751, in that time, they likely did not have a child that
2 CONT
2 CONT was born in 1745. Moreover, the male names for Ebenezer4, John4, and James4 Moons’ (Peleg and
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert’s brothers) children are known. Thus, I believe the best surviving evidence strongly suggest that
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert4 Moon is likely the father of Benoni."
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=308443061-1-501417&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-c4e7966942493f60c56e67b21b9c675c&mrid=1dcd9d3898d8285438b19ef62b5ae2d7 MyH
2 CONC eritage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 16 2016, 0:55:10 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Benoni died in a farm accident by falling off a hay stack at Rushville, Yates County, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT ******************************
2 CONT
2 CONT This cemetery is on the farm that was once owned by Benoni Moon. His young son filled the first grave in the neighborhood, so presumably this was the site, which afterward was used by other nearby families.* Reference: [https://ww
2 CONC w.findagrave.com/memorial/116163187/benoni-moon Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 21 2022, 22:57:10 UTC''
