0 @N6000000000951167026@ NOTE Nathaniel Warren ... Revolutionary and 1812 wars Section, Wt.#60824... It
1 CONT appears that Nathaniel Warren, Sr., while a resident of Jay,Essex, NY
1 CONT enlised and served as a private from Sept. 9, 1814 to Sept. 15,1814 in Cpt.
1 CONT Shubal Summers Co., of NY Militia and was in the battle ofPlattsburg. The
1 CONT records go on to state that in March, 1855 Persis (Sumner)Warren was aged
1 CONT 93. She stated that her sons Horace, Nathan, Orren and Walterwere in the
1 CONT battle of Plattsburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT Revolutionay and 1812 Wars Section Wt. 48984 ... Bounty and landapplication
1 CONT of Horace Warren states that he Horace Warren had taken theplace of his
1 CONT brother Ebenezer, he being ill. He also named other brothers,Itamar,
1 CONT Walter, Nathan and Orren.
1 CONT
1 CONT Nathaniel was in the 1790 census at Wells, Vt; Lland Deed in1792, Wells;
1 CONT Nathaniel and Persis warren were members of the Baptist Churchat Orwell,
1 CONT Rutland VT in 1792; was in 1800, 1820 and 1820 census at Jay,Essex, NY (NB
1 CONT they probably went from Orwell to jay where their 3 youngestsons were born
1 CONT c 1793, 1795, 1799. Later census records in Ohio show thatNathan Jr., Orren
1 CONT and Horace were born in NY). Susan wife of Horace always saidthat they came
1 CONT to Thompson, OH in the fall of 1822.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source: Alice M. Siders
1 CONT
1 CONT There are conflicting references regarding whether or not he wasthe
1 CONT individual who married Persis Sumner (sister of Hannah whomarried Nathan's
1 CONT brother, Jabez.). Some sources including, I beleive, TheMayflower
1 CONT Descendants_ say it was the Nathaniel warren b) 1757 Sharon, Ct,son of
1 CONT Nathaniel and Jemima (Fuller) Warren.
